WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.341 --> 00:00:08.776
♪ Low. tense music ♪

2
00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:10.278
All right. everybody hold on.

3
00:00:11.712 --> 00:00:14.982
A congresswoman was kidnapped
on American soil...

4
00:00:15.049 --> 00:00:16.317
-[gunfire]
-[grunts]

5
00:00:16.384 --> 00:00:17.761
-[Joe] Congresswoman Hernandez?
-Yeah.

6
00:00:17.785 --> 00:00:19.487
Her family killed at the behest

7
00:00:19.553 --> 00:00:21.655
of the Chinese
Ministry of State.

8
00:00:21.722 --> 00:00:23.724
We'd like to get a Lioness
on the ground.

9
00:00:24.525 --> 00:00:25.693
Do it.

10
00:00:25.826 --> 00:00:27.304
What do you know
about the Lioness program?

11
00:00:27.328 --> 00:00:29.297
-Are you a Lioness?
-I run it.

12
00:00:29.363 --> 00:00:31.065
I don't know
if I can trust this girl.

13
00:00:31.165 --> 00:00:32.500
But I know that I can trust you.

14
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:34.102
What's your mission now?

15
00:00:34.202 --> 00:00:36.313
To protect the mission.
From everything. Including you.

16
00:00:36.337 --> 00:00:39.107
We could choose not to fight.
But choosing not to fight

17
00:00:39.207 --> 00:00:41.509
is how warehouses fill up
with children.

18
00:00:41.575 --> 00:00:43.144
[Joe]
I took one in the field.

19
00:00:43.211 --> 00:00:45.546
I'm hunting how to make peace
with walking away for you.

20
00:00:45.646 --> 00:00:48.182
For them. For me.

21
00:00:48.282 --> 00:00:50.218
Well. I hope you find it.

22
00:00:50.318 --> 00:00:51.395
Your father's the mission now.

23
00:00:51.419 --> 00:00:52.553
-Why?
-Because this is

24
00:00:52.653 --> 00:00:54.122
how he survives.

25
00:00:54.222 --> 00:00:56.124
-They know.
-Who's "they"?

26
00:00:56.224 --> 00:00:58.025
[Josie]
CIA

27
00:00:58.126 --> 00:00:59.727
Special Activities.

28
00:00:59.827 --> 00:01:02.330
-[gasps]
-The mission is to show Iran

29
00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:05.833
and China that we aren't the
only nation with an open border.

30
00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:08.336
Do not get yourself caught.

31
00:01:08.402 --> 00:01:10.204
Everyone's watching on this one.

32
00:01:10.304 --> 00:01:11.905
Am I a part of this?

33
00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:13.307
You're the part.

34
00:01:13.407 --> 00:01:15.943
We're gonna find out
how well you fly.

35
00:01:16.043 --> 00:01:17.478
Two minutes to target.

36
00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:21.682
♪ Quiet music ♪

37
00:01:21.749 --> 00:01:23.417
[Neal] I wasn't sure
you were coming home.

38
00:01:23.551 --> 00:01:26.053
I wasn't sure I still had one
to come home to.

39
00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:28.222
[Neal] You always have
one to come home to.

40
00:01:28.322 --> 00:01:29.690
Look who's home!

41
00:01:29.757 --> 00:01:31.091
[Charlie]
Mom? Is that you?

42
00:01:31.192 --> 00:01:33.494
-[Kate] Mom?
-It's me. baby. Oh.

43
00:01:34.895 --> 00:01:37.030
♪ Tense. screeching music ♪

44
00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:38.608
[newswoman 1]
The French government has said

45
00:01:38.632 --> 00:01:40.601
it is considering all options.

46
00:01:40.734 --> 00:01:43.204
including declaring
a state of emergency

47
00:01:43.304 --> 00:01:44.572
after a third night

48
00:01:44.672 --> 00:01:46.440
of escalating
violence and rioting...

49
00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:48.051
[newsman 1] Let's start
with the Middle East.

50
00:01:48.075 --> 00:01:49.286
The Times is reporting
that Hamas

51
00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:50.878
has denied reports that it has

52
00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:52.521
ignored requests from
the international community

53
00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:54.247
concerning the crisis in Gaza...

54
00:01:54.315 --> 00:01:55.991
[newswoman 2] A devastating
scene. meanwhile. in Oaksville.

55
00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:57.918
Several people dead
and even more missing

56
00:01:58.018 --> 00:01:59.698
from an explosion
at an explosives plant...

57
00:01:59.787 --> 00:02:01.865
[newswoman 3] Dozens of fighters
were killed in overnight

58
00:02:01.889 --> 00:02:04.458
border clashes between
Pakistan and Afghanistan

59
00:02:04.592 --> 00:02:06.527
in the most serious
fighting between...

60
00:02:06.627 --> 00:02:08.562
[newswoman 4]
Ukraine's president said Russia

61
00:02:08.662 --> 00:02:10.163
targeted the country

62
00:02:10.264 --> 00:02:11.765
with 450 drones and 30 missiles

63
00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:15.169
in a countrywide attack
targeting the...

64
00:02:15.269 --> 00:02:16.579
[newswoman 5] Well. Max.
we've been on lockdown

65
00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:18.306
here in these capitol buildings

66
00:02:18.406 --> 00:02:20.341
for almost four hours now.

67
00:02:20.441 --> 00:02:23.877
[newswoman 6]
ATF. TBI. Homeland Security.

68
00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:25.946
and several other agencies
are currently...

69
00:02:26.046 --> 00:02:28.091
[newswoman 7] The attorney
general's office in Brazil

70
00:02:28.115 --> 00:02:29.716
has filed an indictment

71
00:02:29.817 --> 00:02:31.628
-against 39 people...
-[newsman 2] The Middle East is

72
00:02:31.652 --> 00:02:32.929
the fulcrum of it all.
we know this. But the thing

73
00:02:32.953 --> 00:02:34.322
could spread like wildfire.

74
00:02:34.422 --> 00:02:36.089
[newswoman 8]
Israel remains in Gaza

75
00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:38.759
and still rejects
a two-state solution.

76
00:02:38.826 --> 00:02:42.263
so is this the dawn
of a new Middle East?

77
00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:48.836
-[Neal] Good morning.
-Good morning.

78
00:02:48.936 --> 00:02:52.172
Oh. good God.
it's freezing. [chuckles]

79
00:02:52.273 --> 00:02:54.608
-It helps with inflammation.
-[Neal] Yeah.

80
00:02:54.708 --> 00:02:55.809
so does Advil. honey.

81
00:02:55.909 --> 00:02:56.986
I don't want a pill to do it.

82
00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.546
I want my body to do it.

83
00:02:58.646 --> 00:03:01.715
Well. I can think of a few
things I want your body to do.

84
00:03:09.357 --> 00:03:12.092
That window closed
about an hour ago.

85
00:03:13.827 --> 00:03:16.530
-There was a window?
-Yeah. and you missed it.

86
00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:17.898
No.

87
00:03:17.998 --> 00:03:20.033
[chuckles]

88
00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:22.403
[music playing faintly]

89
00:03:24.505 --> 00:03:26.182
I thought you finished
your homework last night.

90
00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:27.841
Dad. what's the capital
of Maine?

91
00:03:27.908 --> 00:03:30.644
Uh. capital. uh... Honey.
what's the capital of Maine?

92
00:03:30.744 --> 00:03:32.079
Uh. Augusta.

93
00:03:32.179 --> 00:03:33.447
Mm. That's Georgia.

94
00:03:33.547 --> 00:03:34.958
No. the capital of Georgia's
Atlanta. honey.

95
00:03:34.982 --> 00:03:36.650
She's right.
It's Augusta. Daddy.

96
00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:38.185
Really? Hmm. Never heard of it.

97
00:03:38.286 --> 00:03:41.522
-What about Vermont?
-Vermont. that is Burlington.

98
00:03:41.622 --> 00:03:42.923
Montpelier.

99
00:03:43.023 --> 00:03:44.468
-It's weird that you know that.
-[Kate] How come

100
00:03:44.492 --> 00:03:46.236
-you don't know it. Dad?
-[Neal] Okay. wise guys.

101
00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:48.562
who can name the key nerves
of the thoracic wall?

102
00:03:48.696 --> 00:03:50.430
That's easy.
It's the intercostal nerve...

103
00:03:50.531 --> 00:03:51.575
-You're disqualified.
-[girls laughing]

104
00:03:51.599 --> 00:03:52.866
Why am I disqualified?

105
00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:54.567
You're-you're disqualified.
[chuckles]

106
00:03:54.668 --> 00:03:56.380
[Kate] Okay. wait. wait. wait.
Here's a question. Ready?

107
00:03:56.404 --> 00:03:58.939
X cubed. minus 6X squared.

108
00:03:59.039 --> 00:04:02.410
plus 11X. minus six equals zero.

109
00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:04.244
-What?
-I didn't hear a question.

110
00:04:04.345 --> 00:04:05.846
[Kate]
Okay. question.

111
00:04:05.946 --> 00:04:07.724
What are the variables
that make the equation zero?

112
00:04:07.748 --> 00:04:10.059
No. never in your life will that
have a practical application.

113
00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:11.361
I'm pulling you
from that school.

114
00:04:11.385 --> 00:04:13.754
-[laughs]
-Oh. my God. It's so easy.

115
00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:15.632
-Easy? You're grounded.
-[Kate] Grounded? Really? Why?

116
00:04:15.656 --> 00:04:18.591
I don't know yet.
Are you back for dinner?

117
00:04:18.692 --> 00:04:19.793
I should be.

118
00:04:19.927 --> 00:04:21.695
Could get used to
this nine-to-five thing.

119
00:04:21.795 --> 00:04:23.531
[sighs] Don't.

120
00:04:24.798 --> 00:04:27.200
See you ladies tonight.

121
00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:28.536
Ah. no love for Dad?

122
00:04:28.636 --> 00:04:30.971
I'm saving all my love
for you. Daddy.

123
00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:34.408
-Ew! [groans]
-All right. Gross.

124
00:04:34.508 --> 00:04:35.909
-Gross.
-[Joe] Okay.

125
00:04:35.976 --> 00:04:37.621
-Fine. fine. fine.
-Oh. okay. All right. all right.

126
00:04:37.645 --> 00:04:39.088
-[Kate] Bye. Mom. love you.
-[Charlie] Bye. Mom.

127
00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:41.315
All right. all right.
Finish up. We got to go.

128
00:04:41.449 --> 00:04:43.651
♪ Dramatic music ♪

129
00:04:45.786 --> 00:04:48.021
[birds singing]

130
00:04:54.628 --> 00:04:56.430
[chuckles]

131
00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:58.332
-[sighs]
-Anything interesting?

132
00:04:58.466 --> 00:05:00.668
I never thought the headline
"End of Democracy"

133
00:05:00.801 --> 00:05:02.336
would ring so hollow.

134
00:05:03.103 --> 00:05:05.238
Can only cry "wolf"
so many times.

135
00:05:05.305 --> 00:05:06.907
[sighs] Seems so shortsighted.

136
00:05:06.974 --> 00:05:09.810
An entire industry
rendering itself irrelevant.

137
00:05:09.943 --> 00:05:11.311
Not if you think

138
00:05:11.445 --> 00:05:12.822
about how they were trained
and who trained them.

139
00:05:12.846 --> 00:05:14.882
-Just follow the money.
-Yeah.

140
00:05:14.982 --> 00:05:17.751
Qatar alone has donated
over $11 billion dollars

141
00:05:17.851 --> 00:05:19.653
to U.S. universities.

142
00:05:20.554 --> 00:05:24.792
China has donated
$2.3 billion since 2012.

143
00:05:24.892 --> 00:05:27.661
with $12 billion in tuition paid

144
00:05:27.795 --> 00:05:31.432
for Chinese nationals
at our universities.

145
00:05:31.499 --> 00:05:34.935
And you're surprised that
graduates of those schools are

146
00:05:35.002 --> 00:05:37.337
espousing communist agendas

147
00:05:37.438 --> 00:05:40.073
and declaring
democracy is dying?

148
00:05:41.108 --> 00:05:43.110
That's what
they were trained to say.

149
00:05:43.176 --> 00:05:44.845
Doesn't scare you even a little?

150
00:05:44.945 --> 00:05:46.246
Fool's gold. honey.

151
00:05:46.346 --> 00:05:49.517
You want to scare me.
start talking about AI.

152
00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:51.719
That's the real end
of democracy.

153
00:05:51.852 --> 00:05:53.621
-[phone buzzing]
-Oh.

154
00:05:53.721 --> 00:05:55.022
Hey. you on your way in?

155
00:05:55.122 --> 00:05:56.490
I'll be there in 30. You?

156
00:05:56.590 --> 00:05:58.358
[Meade]
Across town. security brief.

157
00:05:58.492 --> 00:05:59.493
[Joe]
Am I needed?

158
00:05:59.593 --> 00:06:00.828
No. not yet.

159
00:06:00.894 --> 00:06:02.171
[Joe]
We're pretty close over here.

160
00:06:02.195 --> 00:06:04.197
[Meade]
Well. you know the deal.

161
00:06:04.297 --> 00:06:05.297
A lot of red tape

162
00:06:05.332 --> 00:06:06.700
on this side of the fence.

163
00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:08.902
[tires screeching]

164
00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:10.704
[car honks]

165
00:06:10.838 --> 00:06:12.372
-Oh. nice.
-[Meade] What's nice?

166
00:06:12.473 --> 00:06:14.241
[grunts]

167
00:06:16.176 --> 00:06:19.947
Shit! I'm blackjacked!
I'm blackjacked!

168
00:06:23.517 --> 00:06:24.985
[Meade]
Joe?

169
00:06:25.085 --> 00:06:26.386
Joe?

170
00:06:26.487 --> 00:06:28.155
[groans]

171
00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:29.923
[screams]

172
00:06:31.058 --> 00:06:33.927
[screams] Damn it! No!

173
00:06:34.027 --> 00:06:35.729
[grunting]

174
00:06:35.863 --> 00:06:37.731
[Meade]
Blackjack on Raven.

175
00:06:37.831 --> 00:06:40.233
Blackjack on Raven.
unfolding in real time.

176
00:06:40.332 --> 00:06:43.904
Access beacon. Send all assets
to last known location.

177
00:06:44.037 --> 00:06:45.873
[Joe screaming]

178
00:06:45.939 --> 00:06:48.241
♪ suspenseful. dramatic music ♪

179
00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:02.456
♪ dramatic. haunting music ♪

180
00:07:32.553 --> 00:07:35.222
♪♪♪

181
00:08:00.814 --> 00:08:03.083
♪ tense. dramatic music ♪

182
00:08:15.629 --> 00:08:17.731
[security wand whistling]

183
00:08:33.847 --> 00:08:34.881
Where's the park?

184
00:08:34.982 --> 00:08:36.415
[Meade]
Georgetown campus.

185
00:08:37.684 --> 00:08:38.818
How'd this come our way?

186
00:08:38.919 --> 00:08:40.220
Approached Kyle at a bar.

187
00:08:40.352 --> 00:08:42.422
-What bar?
-The Net. He thought he was

188
00:08:42.522 --> 00:08:44.825
being honeypotted.
She said she saw him in Kiev

189
00:08:44.892 --> 00:08:47.360
with 46 and then at
the Ukraine embassy last week.

190
00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:52.165
She's FISU. worked her way
into Russia's SVR 2018.

191
00:08:52.265 --> 00:08:54.305
-Long time to double agent.
-We reached out to Kiev.

192
00:08:54.334 --> 00:08:56.637
-FISU verified it.
-Okay.

193
00:08:56.737 --> 00:08:58.538
So what does she have?

194
00:08:58.672 --> 00:09:01.909
Pretty curious
about that myself.

195
00:09:04.011 --> 00:09:06.246
♪ Tense. suspenseful music ♪

196
00:09:23.530 --> 00:09:24.898
[panting]

197
00:09:37.945 --> 00:09:39.613
We good?

198
00:09:40.447 --> 00:09:41.849
You're good.

199
00:09:58.732 --> 00:10:00.634
It's not how
we like to do things.

200
00:10:00.734 --> 00:10:04.071
SVR watches their own
more than they watch you.

201
00:10:04.872 --> 00:10:06.783
We've been looking for a way
since the war started.

202
00:10:06.807 --> 00:10:08.709
An opportunity appeared.
I took it.

203
00:10:08.776 --> 00:10:09.776
Okay.

204
00:10:09.843 --> 00:10:12.112
What are you gonna do about it?

205
00:10:13.446 --> 00:10:14.948
Aleksi Yurimov.

206
00:10:15.048 --> 00:10:17.885
I'm sorry. I'm not up
on my Russian spies.

207
00:10:17.951 --> 00:10:19.619
The Middle East is my theater.

208
00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:21.321
-You know SSD?
-Yes.

209
00:10:21.454 --> 00:10:22.622
He runs it.

210
00:10:23.423 --> 00:10:26.860
He's moved to the front.
I have his location.

211
00:10:29.229 --> 00:10:32.132
Okay. Yay for you.

212
00:10:33.100 --> 00:10:34.902
We want you to have him.

213
00:10:35.736 --> 00:10:37.637
Why would we want that?

214
00:10:38.772 --> 00:10:41.141
Leverage. Maybe you trade him.

215
00:10:42.743 --> 00:10:44.644
Why would you want that?

216
00:10:45.478 --> 00:10:46.914
He's Putin's hammer.

217
00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:50.918
If we kill him. Putin's
retaliation will be severe.

218
00:10:51.018 --> 00:10:53.353
But if you take him.
it's just the game.

219
00:10:53.486 --> 00:10:56.289
And a big risk to a unit
or a Ground Branch detail

220
00:10:56.389 --> 00:10:57.925
that gets trotted
before the world

221
00:10:58.025 --> 00:10:59.626
on their way to a gulag
if they fail.

222
00:10:59.693 --> 00:11:03.463
You'd be taking Putin's queen
off the chessboard.

223
00:11:03.563 --> 00:11:05.665
Do you understand the value
of that for all of us?

224
00:11:05.766 --> 00:11:09.703
Oh. I understand. For you.

225
00:11:09.837 --> 00:11:11.504
But what do we get in return?

226
00:11:12.305 --> 00:11:14.274
-What do you want?
-I don't know. What do you do?

227
00:11:14.374 --> 00:11:16.877
-What's your field?
-Recruitment and infiltration.

228
00:11:16.977 --> 00:11:18.378
You know honeypot?

229
00:11:18.511 --> 00:11:21.849
Mm. I know honeypot.

230
00:11:21.949 --> 00:11:24.417
I hold the jar.

231
00:11:26.019 --> 00:11:27.354
How do we contact you?

232
00:11:27.454 --> 00:11:29.522
Give me your number.
I'll have someone con...

233
00:11:29.656 --> 00:11:31.658
Not on your fucking life.

234
00:11:31.725 --> 00:11:35.963
You give contact to me.
and we'll reach out. Maybe.

235
00:11:36.029 --> 00:11:37.264
[Oleksandra sighs]

236
00:11:40.167 --> 00:11:42.870
Only good for a week.

237
00:11:48.075 --> 00:11:51.879
If we're interested.
we'll be in touch.

238
00:11:51.979 --> 00:11:55.115
♪ Tense. dramatic music ♪

239
00:12:14.034 --> 00:12:16.303
[tires screech]

240
00:12:26.579 --> 00:12:27.815
Go smooth?

241
00:12:27.915 --> 00:12:30.183
-Mm. it was interesting.
-[Two Cups] Oh. yeah?

242
00:12:30.283 --> 00:12:32.185
Where does "interesting"
send us?

243
00:12:32.285 --> 00:12:33.887
Ever been to Ukraine?

244
00:12:33.954 --> 00:12:36.256
[groans]
You got to be kidding me. boss.

245
00:12:36.356 --> 00:12:39.960
Uh. you know. Ukraine is on the
bucket list there. chief-eroni.

246
00:12:40.060 --> 00:12:41.795
Yeah. I think it is now.

247
00:12:41.895 --> 00:12:43.931
[Bobby]
Fuck.

248
00:12:44.798 --> 00:12:46.033
[Bobby sighs]

249
00:12:49.536 --> 00:12:51.771
[indistinct radio chatter]

250
00:13:11.624 --> 00:13:14.995
♪ tense. suspenseful music ♪

251
00:13:41.221 --> 00:13:43.390
[drones buzzing]

252
00:13:59.339 --> 00:14:00.540
[gunfire]

253
00:14:02.910 --> 00:14:05.112
[gunfire continues]

254
